    "ai_summary": "### 🧠 تحليل DeepSeek-R1 (MITRE & STRIDE Model):\n<think>\nOkay, so I'm looking at this analysis of the website https://httpbin.org, and there are several security issues mentioned. I need to understand each of these points to figure out what's going wrong and how to fix them. Let me go through each one step by step.\n\nFirst, there's a critical issue about the CSP being missing. CSP stands for Content Security Policy, right? It's used to prevent XSS attacks because it tells the browser which sources of content are allowed to load. If it's missing, that means any scripts could potentially be injected into the site, which is bad. So, the site is vulnerable to XSS attacks because of this.\n\nNext, there's a high issue about missing clickjacking protection. Clickjacking is when an attacker tricks a user into clicking something they didn't intend to, like a button on another site. Without protection, this site could be embedded in a frame or iframe, making clickjacking possible. That's a serious issue because it can lead to unauthorized actions by users.\n\nAnother high issue is that HSTS is missing. HSTS stands for HTTP Strict Transport Security, and it forces the browser to use HTTPS even if the user types in HTTP. Without HSTS, an attacker could perform a man\n\n---\n### 🥷 تحليل GLM Security Engine (Remediation & Patches):\nBased on the given website <https://httpbin.org>, here is the suggested code snippet for implementing the WAF rules with Forward Compatible CSP and Clickjacking protection:\n\n1. CSP (Content Security Policy)\n\n```python\nContent-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'unsafe-eval' 'https://apis.google.com' 'https://www.gstatic.com'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: 'https://fonts.googleapis.com' 'https://www.google-analytics.com'; font-src 'self' 'https://fonts.gstatic.com'; connect-src 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none';\n```\n\n2. Clickjacking Protection\n\n```python\nX-Frame-Options: DENY\nX-XSS-Protection: 1; mode=block\nX-Content-Type-Options: nosniff\nX-Permitted-Cross-Domain-Policies: none\n```\n\n3. HST",
